docs/DEPLOYMENT.md :: retarget :: - **Dead letters:** `processor_cli dlq list | show <id> | drop <id>` (§ `/etc/processor/`). There is no replay. An entry failed to decode, was not a command, or is a command that raised outside the handler on every attempt (`reason` starts `gave up on attempt`): that one is a bug to fix. Before dead-lettering such a command, Processor published a terminal `dead_lettered` whose `detail` starts `dead-lettered:` (best effort), so Watcher has closed it (#17; `extraction_error` before co-core 0.37.0, #21). The journal's `dead-lettering` record says which: `failure_fact` is `published`, `skipped` (a fact had already gone out) or `refused`. On a command given up at the cap, `handle_skipped` is `true` when the record retries a give-up that did not finish (the failure fact refused transiently, or the dead-letter refused), with no re-run of the command and the original traceback (#28). The same entry logging that every ~11 min while it stays pending means `content.process.dlq` refuses it: `journalctl -u processor -o cat | jq -cR 'fromjson? | select(.handle_skipped) | {timestamp, command_id, message_id, reason}'`.
